/-!
# Surjectivity of the canonical map onto the normalized dualizing module of the blowup

In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B4W] with `A` not regular, let `ω_A` be a dualizing module for `A`,
let `f : X ⟶ Spec(A)` be the blowup in the maximal ideal with exceptional divisor `i : E ⟶ X`, and
let `ω_X` be the dualizing module of `X` normalized relative to `ω_A`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation.DualizingNormalization`, [Stacks, Remark 0B4R]).
Clause (3) of [Stacks, Tag 0B64] says that the canonical map `f^*ω_A ⟶ ω_X` of
[Stacks, Tag 0BBU] (`AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation.normalizedPullbackMap`) is
surjective.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.epi_normalizedPullbackMap`: **clause (3) of
  [Stacks, Tag 0B64]**, at the source's hypotheses.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.range_exceptionalImmersion`: the exceptional divisor is the
  fibre over the closed point.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation.surjective_appTop_normalizedPullbackMap`: the
  canonical map is split, hence surjective, on global sections.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.epi_of_surjective_appTop_of_generatingSections`: a map
  `f^*ω_A ⟶ ω_X` onto a dualizing module that is surjective on global sections is an
  epimorphism once `ω_X|_E` is generated by its global sections.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_of_isoAlgebraicClosure`:
  `ω_X|_E` is generated by its global sections, by [Stacks, Tag 0B5H] at `E` over `κ`, given
  [Stacks, Tag 0E32] at `E`, which is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.pullbackDualizingSheafOverFieldIso`.

## The argument

This is the source's proof. Clause (1) of the tag gives `ω_X|_E ≅ ω_E ⊗ 𝒪_E(1)`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.nonempty_pullback_iso_dualizingSheafOverField_twist`), which is
generated by its global sections by [Stacks, Tag 0B5H]: `𝒪_E(1)` is very ample (clause (2) of
[Stacks, Tag 0B63]) of degree at least two (clause (3) of that tag, `A` not being regular). A
module on `E` generated by global sections has `H¹(E, -(n)) = 0` for `n ≥ 0`, so clause (2) of
the tag gives `H¹(X, ω_X(1)) = 0`, and the restriction sequence
`0 ⟶ ω_X(1) ⟶ ω_X ⟶ i_*(ω_X|_E) ⟶ 0` makes `Γ(X, ω_X) ⟶ Γ(E, ω_X|_E)` surjective. The canonical
map is surjective on global sections because `Γ(X, ω_X) = ω_A` is used to define it
([Stacks, Tag 0BBU]); so the generators of `ω_X|_E` lift to global sections of `f^*ω_A`, the
canonical map is surjective after restriction to `E`, and since `ω_X` is of finite type, `f` is
proper and `A` is local, it is surjective (the cokernel is detected on the closed fibre). The
source phrases this last step as "`ω_X` is globally generated".

Here the arguments of clause (2) and of the closed-fibre detection are applied to the canonical
map of `NormalizedDualizingTrace.lean`, for the `ω_X` of [Stacks, Remark 0B4R].

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B64](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B64)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BBU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BBU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5H](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5H)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B63](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B63)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B4R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B4R)
-/

-- This file uses the locally small derived-category models below, which are not
-- global instances (see `StacksFrontier.Homology.DerivedCategory.LocallySmall`):
-- `D(𝒪_X)` for a scheme.
attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.HyperplaneTwistSequence
open Stacks.Cohomology.FormalFunctions (cohomologyDeltaFunctor)

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

namespace RationalSingularitySituation

variable (S : RationalSingularitySituation.{u}) [IsLocallyNoetherian S.X]
  {ωA : ModuleCat.{u} S.A} {ωX : S.X.Modules}

/-- **The canonical map of [Stacks, Tag 0BBU] is split on global sections.** The unit of
`globalSectionsAdjunction` at `ω_A`, preceded by the trace, is a section of
`H⁰(X, f^*ω_A) ⟶ H⁰(X, ω_X)`: the adjunct of the canonical map is the inverse trace. -/
theorem normalizedPullbackMap_globalSections_split
    (hωA : Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingRingModule S.A ωA)
    (e : (S.relativeDualizingComplex ωA).obj ≅
      (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor S.X.Modules 0).obj ωX) :
    ((S.normalizedTraceIso hωA e).hom ≫ S.globalSectionsAdjunction.unit.app ωA) ≫
        (Scheme.Modules.pushforward S.f ⋙ moduleSpecΓFunctor).map
          (S.normalizedPullbackMap hωA e) =
      𝟙 ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward S.f ⋙ moduleSpecΓFunctor).obj ωX) := by
  rw [Category.assoc, normalizedPullbackMap, ← Adjunction.homEquiv_unit, Equiv.apply_symm_apply,
    Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc]
  rfl

/-- **Every global section of `ω_X` is the image of a global section of `f^*ω_A`** under the
canonical map of [Stacks, Tag 0BBU], which is split on global sections. -/
theorem surjective_appTop_normalizedPullbackMap
    (hωA : Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingRingModule S.A ωA)
    (e : (S.relativeDualizingComplex ωA).obj ≅
      (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor S.X.Modules 0).obj ωX) :
    Function.Surjective ((S.normalizedPullbackMap hωA e).val.app (op ⊤)) := fun y =>
  ⟨((S.normalizedTraceIso hωA e).hom ≫ S.globalSectionsAdjunction.unit.app ωA).hom y,
    congrArg (fun k => k.hom y) (S.normalizedPullbackMap_globalSections_split hωA e)⟩

end RationalSingularitySituation

namespace BlowUpDualizing

/-! ### The exceptional divisor is the fibre over the closed point -/

/-- **The exceptional divisor of the blowup at the maximal ideal is the fibre over the closed
point.** The image of a closed subscheme is the support of its sheaf of ideals, the support of an
inverse-image ideal sheaf is the inverse image of the support, and the support of the sheaf of
ideals of the closed point is the closed point. -/
theorem range_exceptionalImmersion (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] :
    Set.range (exceptionalImmersion A).base =
      (blowUpToBase (centre A)).base ⁻¹' {IsLocalRing.closedPoint A} := by
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι,
    show exceptionalIdeal (centre A) = (centre A).comap (blowUpToBase (centre A)) from rfl,
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap, TopologicalSpace.Closeds.coe_preimage]
  exact congrArg (fun T : Set (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) =>
    (blowUpToBase (centre A)).base ⁻¹' T) (supportSet_ker_residuePoint A)

variable (S : RationalSingularitySituation.{u})

/-! ### Generation along `E` gives surjectivity -/

/-- **A map `f^*ω_A ⟶ ω_X` onto a dualizing module of the blowup that is surjective on global
sections is an epimorphism once `ω_X|_E` is generated by its global sections.**

A module on `E` generated by its global sections has `H¹(E, -(n)) = 0` for all `n ≥ 0`
(`isZero_firstCohomology_curveTwist_of_generatingSections`), so `H¹(X, ω_X(1)) = 0` by
clause (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0B64] in the form
`isZero_firstCohomology_dualizingTwist_of_restrictionVanishing`; the restriction sequence then
makes `Γ(X, ω_X) ⟶ Γ(E, ω_X|_E)` surjective. The generators of `ω_X|_E` therefore lift to global
sections of `ω_X` and then of `f^*ω_A`, so `φ` is an epimorphism after restriction to `E`; since
`ω_X` is of finite type, `f` is proper and `A` is local, that suffices
(`Scheme.Modules.epi_of_epi_pullback_of_range_eq_fibre`). -/
theorem epi_of_surjective_appTop_of_generatingSections (ωA : ModuleCat.{u} S.A)
    (ωX : (blowUpScheme S.A).Modules)
    (hωX : letI : IsLocallyNoetherian (blowUpScheme S.A) := isLocallyNoetherian_blowUpScheme S.A
      Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingModule ωX)
    (φ : (Scheme.Modules.pullback (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).f).obj (tilde ωA) ⟶ ωX)
    (hφ : Function.Surjective (φ.val.app (op ⊤)))
    (G : SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (exceptionalImmersion S.A)).obj ωX)) :
    Epi φ := by
  let : IsLocallyNoetherian (blowUpScheme S.A) := isLocallyNoetherian_blowUpScheme S.A
  let : IsProper (blowUpToBase (centre S.A)) := isProper_blowUpToBase (centre S.A)
  have hft : ωX.IsFiniteType := hωX.1.isFiniteType
  -- the restriction sequence, with the canonical restriction map as its second map
  obtain ⟨fseq, w, hS⟩ := exists_shortExact_schemeTwist_dualizing_unit S.A ωX hωX
  -- the curve vanishing `H¹(E, (ω_X|_E)(n)) = 0`, from the global generation `G`
  have hcurve : ∀ n : ℕ, IsZero (((cohomologyDeltaFunctor (exceptionalCurve S.A)).functor 1).obj
      (curveTwist S.A ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (exceptionalImmersion S.A)).obj ωX) (n : ℤ))) :=
    fun n => isZero_firstCohomology_curveTwist_of_generatingSections S _ G n
  -- `H¹(X, ω_X(1)) = 0`, in the group-valued cohomology the long exact sequence is extracted for
  have h₂ := isZero_firstCohomology_dualizingTwist_of_restrictionVanishing S.A ωX hωX hcurve 1
  rw [Nat.cast_one] at h₂
  have hH : IsZero (Hgroup (blowUpScheme S.A).ringCatSheaf ⊤ 1 (schemeTwist S.A ωX 1)) :=
    (Stacks.Cohomology.CechAcyclic.isZero_rightDerived_evaluation_iff_isZero_Hgroup
      (blowUpScheme S.A).ringCatSheaf ⊤ 1 _).1 h₂
  -- global sections of `ω_X` restrict onto global sections of `ω_X|_E`
  have hsurj := Stacks.SerreAffinenessCriterion.surjective_app_of_isZero_hgroup_one
    (blowUpScheme S.A) ⊤ hS hH
  -- each generator of `ω_X|_E` lifts to a global section of `f^*ω_A`, restricted to `E`
  have hlift : ∀ j : G.I, ∃ b : SheafOfModules.sections
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (exceptionalImmersion S.A)).obj
        ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).f).obj (tilde ωA))),
      SheafOfModules.sectionsMap ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (exceptionalImmersion S.A)).map φ) b =
        G.s j := by
    intro j
    obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := Scheme.Modules.exists_restrictSections_eq
      (exceptionalImmersion S.A) ωX hsurj (G.s j)
    obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := Scheme.Modules.exists_sections_eq_of_surjective_app_top φ hφ t
    exact ⟨Scheme.Modules.restrictSections (exceptionalImmersion S.A) _ b,
      ((Scheme.Modules.sectionsMap_restrictSections (exceptionalImmersion S.A) φ b).trans
          (congrArg (Scheme.Modules.restrictSections (exceptionalImmersion S.A) ωX) hb)).trans ht⟩
  choose s hs using hlift
  exact Scheme.Modules.epi_of_epi_pullback_of_range_eq_fibre
    (blowUpToBase (centre S.A)) (exceptionalImmersion S.A) (range_exceptionalImmersion S.A) _ hft
    (Scheme.Modules.epi_of_sections_lift _ G s hs)

/-! ### Global generation of `ω_X|_E` -/

/-- **The dualizing sheaf of the exceptional curve over `κ` is coherent**, for `ω_X` normalized
relative to `ω_A`: it is `(ω_X|_E)(-1)` by clause (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0B64], and `ω_X` is
coherent. -/
theorem isCoherent_dualizingSheafOverField_exceptionalDivisor
    (ωA : ModuleCat.{u} S.A) (hωA : Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingRingModule S.A ωA)
    (ωX : (blowUpScheme S.A).Modules)
    (N : letI : IsLocallyNoetherian (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).X :=
        isLocallyNoetherian_blowUpScheme S.A
      (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).DualizingNormalization ωA ωX) :
    (Stacks.Duality.dualizingSheafOverField
      (X := (cohenMacaulayCurveSituationExceptionalDivisor S).X)
      (cohenMacaulayCurveSituationExceptionalDivisor S).f).IsCoherent := by
  let : IsLocallyNoetherian (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).X :=
    isLocallyNoetherian_blowUpScheme S.A
  let : IsLocallyNoetherian (blowUpScheme S.A) := isLocallyNoetherian_blowUpScheme S.A
  let : IsLocallyNoetherian (exceptionalCurve S.A) := isLocallyNoetherian_exceptionalCurve S.A
  let : ωX.IsCoherent := N.isDualizing.1
  let : ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (exceptionalImmersion S.A)).obj ωX).IsCoherent :=
    isCoherent_pullback (exceptionalImmersion S.A) ωX
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := nonempty_dualizingSheafOverField_iso_curveTwist S ωA hωA ωX N
  exact Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IrreducibleDevissage.isCoherent_of_iso' e
    (SheafOfModules.isCoherent_tensorSheaf_of_isInvertible (exceptionalCurve S.A) _
      (curveTwistSheaf S.A (-1)))

/-- **`ω_X|_E` is generated by its global sections**, for `ω_X` normalized relative to `ω_A`:
[Stacks, Tag 0B5H] at the exceptional curve over `κ`, through `ω_X|_E ≅ ω_E ⊗ 𝒪_E(1)` (clause (1)
of [Stacks, Tag 0B64]), `𝒪_E(1)` being very ample (clause (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0B63]) of degree at
least two (clause (3) of that tag, as `A` is not regular).

The input `e` is [Stacks, Tag 0E32] at `E`, the compatibility of the dualizing sheaf of `E` with
the extension `κ ⊆ κ̄`, through which the general-field case of [Stacks, Tag 0B5H] reduces to the
algebraically closed one. -/
theorem nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_of_isoAlgebraicClosure
    (hnot : ¬ IsRegularLocalRing S.A)
    (ωA : ModuleCat.{u} S.A) (hωA : Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingRingModule S.A ωA)
    (ωX : (blowUpScheme S.A).Modules)
    (N : letI : IsLocallyNoetherian (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).X :=
        isLocallyNoetherian_blowUpScheme S.A
      (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).DualizingNormalization ωA ωX)
    (e : (Scheme.Modules.pullback
          (cohenMacaulayCurveSituationExceptionalDivisor S).algebraicClosureProj).obj
          (Stacks.Duality.dualizingSheafOverField
            (X := (cohenMacaulayCurveSituationExceptionalDivisor S).X)
            (cohenMacaulayCurveSituationExceptionalDivisor S).f) ≅
        Stacks.Duality.dualizingSheafOverField
          (X := (cohenMacaulayCurveSituationExceptionalDivisor S).algebraicClosure.X)
          (cohenMacaulayCurveSituationExceptionalDivisor S).algebraicClosure.f) :
    Nonempty ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (exceptionalImmersion S.A)).obj ωX).GeneratingSections := by
  obtain ⟨g⟩ := nonempty_pullback_iso_dualizingSheafOverField_twist S ωA hωA ωX N
  obtain ⟨G⟩ := (cohenMacaulayCurveSituationExceptionalDivisor S)
    |>.nonempty_generatingSections_dualizing_tensorSheaf_of_isoAlgebraicClosure
      (curveTwistSheaf S.A 1) (isRelativelyVeryAmple_curveTwistSheaf_one S.A)
      (two_le_invertibleCurveDegree_curveTwistSheaf_one S hnot)
      (isCoherent_dualizingSheafOverField_exceptionalDivisor S ωA hωA ωX N) e
  exact ⟨SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections.equivOfIso g.symm G⟩

/-! ### Clause (3) -/

/-- **The canonical map `f^*ω_A ⟶ ω_X` of [Stacks, Tag 0BBU] is surjective once `ω_X|_E` is
generated by its global sections**, for `ω_X` normalized relative to `ω_A`: it is surjective on
global sections (`surjective_appTop_normalizedPullbackMap`), and
`epi_of_surjective_appTop_of_generatingSections` applies. -/
theorem epi_normalizedPullbackMap_of_generatingSections
    (ωA : ModuleCat.{u} S.A) (hωA : Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingRingModule S.A ωA)
    (ωX : (blowUpScheme S.A).Modules)
    (N : letI : IsLocallyNoetherian (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).X :=
        isLocallyNoetherian_blowUpScheme S.A
      (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).DualizingNormalization ωA ωX)
    (G : SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (exceptionalImmersion S.A)).obj ωX)) :
    letI : IsLocallyNoetherian (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).X :=
      isLocallyNoetherian_blowUpScheme S.A
    Epi ((rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).normalizedPullbackMap hωA N.normalizedIso) := by
  let : IsLocallyNoetherian (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).X :=
    isLocallyNoetherian_blowUpScheme S.A
  exact epi_of_surjective_appTop_of_generatingSections S ωA ωX N.isDualizing _
    ((rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).surjective_appTop_normalizedPullbackMap hωA
      N.normalizedIso) G

/-- **Clause (3) of [Stacks, Tag 0B64], over the [Stacks, Tag 0E32] input at `E`.** In Situation
[Stacks, Tag 0B4W] with `A` not regular, for `ω_A` a dualizing module for `A` and `ω_X` the
dualizing module of the blowup normalized relative to `ω_A`, the canonical map `f^*ω_A ⟶ ω_X` of
[Stacks, Tag 0BBU] is surjective, granted the compatibility `e` of the dualizing sheaf of `E`
with the extension `κ ⊆ κ̄` through which [Stacks, Tag 0B5H] over `κ` is reduced to `κ̄`. -/
theorem epi_normalizedPullbackMap_of_isoAlgebraicClosure
    (hnot : ¬ IsRegularLocalRing S.A)
    (ωA : ModuleCat.{u} S.A) (hωA : Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingRingModule S.A ωA)
    (ωX : (blowUpScheme S.A).Modules)
    (N : letI : IsLocallyNoetherian (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).X :=
        isLocallyNoetherian_blowUpScheme S.A
      (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).DualizingNormalization ωA ωX)
    (e : (Scheme.Modules.pullback
          (cohenMacaulayCurveSituationExceptionalDivisor S).algebraicClosureProj).obj
          (Stacks.Duality.dualizingSheafOverField
            (X := (cohenMacaulayCurveSituationExceptionalDivisor S).X)
            (cohenMacaulayCurveSituationExceptionalDivisor S).f) ≅
        Stacks.Duality.dualizingSheafOverField
          (X := (cohenMacaulayCurveSituationExceptionalDivisor S).algebraicClosure.X)
          (cohenMacaulayCurveSituationExceptionalDivisor S).algebraicClosure.f) :
    letI : IsLocallyNoetherian (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).X :=
      isLocallyNoetherian_blowUpScheme S.A
    Epi ((rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).normalizedPullbackMap hωA N.normalizedIso) :=
  epi_normalizedPullbackMap_of_generatingSections S ωA hωA ωX N
    (nonempty_generatingSections_pullback_of_isoAlgebraicClosure S hnot ωA hωA ωX N e).some

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0B64], clause (3).** In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B4W] assume `A` is not
regular, let `ω_A` be a dualizing module for `A`, let `X` be the blowup of `Spec(A)` in the
maximal ideal and let `ω_X` be the dualizing module of `X`, normalized relative to `ω_A` as in
[Stacks, Remark 0B4R] (`DualizingNormalization`: `ω_X` is dualizing and `f^!(ω_A) ≅ ω_X` in
degree zero). Then the canonical map `f^*ω_A ⟶ ω_X` of [Stacks, Tag 0BBU]
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RationalSingularitySituation.normalizedPullbackMap`) is surjective.

The source's proof: `ω_X|_E ≅ ω_E ⊗ 𝒪_E(1)` (clause (1)) is globally generated by
[Stacks, Tag 0B5H], reduced to `κ̄` through [Stacks, Tag 0E32]
(`CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.pullbackDualizingSheafOverFieldIso`); `H¹(X, ω_X(1)) = 0` lifts its
generators to `Γ(X, ω_X) = ω_A`, and an epimorphism onto `ω_X` is detected on the closed
fibre. -/
@[stacks 0B64 "clause (3) in Situation 0B4W with A not regular: for omega_A a dualizing module \
for A and omega_X the dualizing module of the blowup X of Spec(A) in the maximal ideal, \
normalized relative to omega_A as in Remark 0B4R (DualizingNormalization: omega_X dualizing with \
f^!(omega_A) = omega_X in degree zero), the canonical map f^*omega_A -> omega_X of Tag 0BBU \
(normalizedPullbackMap) is surjective. The source's route: Tag 0B5H at E (via Tag 0E32 to \
kappa-bar, clause (2) of Tag 0B63 for very ampleness, clause (3) of Tag 0B63 for the degree) \
gives global generation of omega_X|_E = omega_E(1) (clause (1)); H^1(X, omega_X(1)) = 0 \
(clause (2), from that generation) lifts it to Gamma(X, omega_X) = omega_A; surjectivity is \
detected on the closed fibre. Nothing is carried"]
theorem epi_normalizedPullbackMap
    (hnot : ¬ IsRegularLocalRing S.A)
    (ωA : ModuleCat.{u} S.A) (hωA : Stacks.Duality.IsDualizingRingModule S.A ωA)
    (ωX : (blowUpScheme S.A).Modules)
    (N : letI : IsLocallyNoetherian (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).X :=
        isLocallyNoetherian_blowUpScheme S.A
      (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).DualizingNormalization ωA ωX) :
    letI : IsLocallyNoetherian (rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).X :=
      isLocallyNoetherian_blowUpScheme S.A
    Epi ((rationalSingularitySituationBlowUp S).normalizedPullbackMap hωA N.normalizedIso) :=
  epi_normalizedPullbackMap_of_isoAlgebraicClosure S hnot ωA hωA ωX N
    (CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.pullbackDualizingSheafOverFieldIso
      (cohenMacaulayCurveSituationExceptionalDivisor S)
      (AlgebraicClosure (cohenMacaulayCurveSituationExceptionalDivisor S).k))

/-! ### Clause (2) -/

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0B64], clause (2).** In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B4W] assume `A` is not
regular, let `ω_A` be a dualizing module for `A`, let `X` be the blowup of `Spec(A)` in the
maximal ideal and let `ω_X` be the dualizing module of `X`, normalized relative to `ω_A` as in
[Stacks, Remark 0B4R] (`DualizingNormalization`). Then `H¹(X, ω_X(n)) = 0` for every `n ≥ 0`.

The source's proof: `ω_X|_E ≅ ω_E ⊗ 𝒪_E(1)` (clause (1)) is generated by its global sections by
[Stacks, Tag 0B5H] (reduced to `κ̄` through [Stacks, Tag 0E32],
`CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.pullbackDualizingSheafOverFieldIso`), so its twists `(ω_X|_E)(n)`,
`n ≥ 0`, have no first cohomology (`isZero_firstCohomology_curveTwist_of_generatingSections`,
from clause (4) of [Stacks, Tag 0B63]); the restriction sequence and the eventual vanishing of
